    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8404": {
      "title": "Public Safety",
      "description": "Public Safety - Lieutenant | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Public Safety - Lieutenant Req #936 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Monday, November 16, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary To provide for the safety and security of all members of the University community. To provide for the physical security of University property & enforce University and Departmental rules and regulations.  Oversee the daily functions of DPS officers and contract security officers to ensure all services are delivered in a consistent, professional, and timely manner. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Position will have operational and administrative oversight of assigned shift(s). Must embrace a community policing/problem-solving approach to patrol responsibilities. Must be capable of Patrolling University properties via foot, bicycle, or vehicle. Plan, supervise, and review the activities of all shift personnel, including shift officers, regarding duties, posts, patrol areas, and dispatch to achieve maximum resource efficiency. Conduct daily shift-level briefing sessions and line inspections to ensure all personnel are properly informed and properly equipped to perform their daily duties. Supervise and direct front-line Public Safety officer response to calls for service and emergency incidents, including, but not limited to, fire alarms/fires, medical incidents, weather emergencies, motor vehicle accidents, disturbances, altercations, etc. May issue Timely Warnings or Crime Notices to the community in compliance with Clery Act mandates. Adheres to the University and the Department of Public Safety’s rules, regulations, responsibilities, and procedures and ensures all assigned personnel do so as well. Complies with and is respectful of Superiors and their instructions, directives, and assignments. Keep superiors informed of performance or personnel issues and initiate and/or carry out appropriate corrective action, counseling, and training. Submits thorough and timely reports documenting any personnel matters, unusual occurrences, complaints, and/or crimes/incidents. Maintains a professional, formal, and approachable demeanor while on duty to foster effective public relations while interacting within the University community. Provide aid or services to the University community, including personal safety escorts, motor vehicle assistance, and room/bldg. locking/unlocking, bank runs, etc. … Interact professionally with all internal University members and external municipal partners/agencies (police, fire, ambulance, etc.). May be required to work special assignments, events, shifts, and extended hours depending upon the needs of the agency. May be required to fulfill Dispatch duties if needed. Assist in the development and delivery of safety and emergency management training programs for department personnel and the university community. Will not act, either on duty or off duty, in any manner that is detrimental, in the view of SHU, to the Mission or reputation of Sacred Heart University. Must maintain all applicable certifications and licensing, including firearm requirements, training, and ongoing qualifications. Essential physical job tasks include sitting, standing, or walking for sustained periods of time; climbing up/downstairs; bending, turning, reaching, and grasping. Visual acuity sufficient for reading ID cards/written materials, Hearing sufficient for perceiving sounds at normal speaking levels. Be able to work in various positions, including but not limited to stooping, standing, bending over, sitting, kneeling, and squatting for extended periods of time. Be able to lift (indicate the weight minimum), pull, and push materials and equipment to complete the assigned job task. May be required to work in extreme outdoor weather conditions (heat, snow, ice, rain, etc.). Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes Associate degree in Criminal Justice or related field. Appropriate Law Enforcement experience may be substituted for a degree. Minimum of ten years of law enforcement or military experience required, or comparable public security experience. Minimum of two years serving in a supervisory level law enforcement position or comparable leadership position in a non-law enforcement agency. Must have separated from law enforcement/military service in good standing. Must hold a valid State Driver’s License and maintain a satisfactory driving record. Possess and maintain: CT State Security Guard Card and Class 1 License endorsement, or other comparable certification as may be required. If former LEO must be capable of meeting standards established by the Law Enforcement Officer’s Safety Act (HR-218). Proficiency in Microsoft Office products (including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. EMR/EMT certification Essential physical job tasks include walking, climbing stairs, driving emergency vehicles, conducting foot patrols in buildings, parking lots, and campus fields, and standing or moving for extended periods.  Breaking up fights or preventing physical altercations. Directing large crowds during events or emergencies. Positioning barricades or moving equipment to manage public spaces and checkpoints.  Directing traffic flow and setting up detours or roadblocks. Carrying and using protective gear and fire extinguishers. Administering CPR or first aid or using automated external defibrillators (AEDs). Carrying medical supplies to assist during emergencies and transporting patients or individuals needing help. Unusual Working Conditions May require working different shifts at various university campuses or facilities. May require working on weekends, holidays, and in adverse weather conditions. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes § 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $51,750 - $66,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Associate Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8393": {
      "title": "Management - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Management - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Management - Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Req #942 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Management in the Welch College of Business & Technology invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Management, beginning Fall 2027 , pending final budgetary approval. We seek an engaged scholar and educator specializing in Entrepreneurship, Strategy, or Innovation who is passionate about creating an exceptional student experience and contributing to the department's innovative and entrepreneurial culture. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research, teaching, or professional interests include artificial intelligence, technology management, and emerging technologies, and who can contribute to the development of new courses, programs, and student experiences in these areas. The Department of Management brings together faculty with expertise in strategy, organizational behavior, entrepreneurship, innovation, human resource management, operations and supply chain management, business law, and international management. The department offers a B.S. in Management, supports several undergraduate minors, and contributes to the College's MBA program. Across these programs, faculty emphasize rigorous scholarship, student-centered teaching, and active, experiential learning. Faculty also have opportunities to connect teaching, scholarship, and community engagement through initiatives such as the Pioneer Pitch Competition , the peer-reviewed New England Journal of Entrepreneurship , and collaborations with SHU's Center for Nonprofits . Teaching & Student Engagement: Excellence in teaching is central to the department’s mission. We seek candidates who create engaging, rigorous learning environments that strengthen students’ critical thinking, leadership, ethical reasoning, and managerial decision-making. Teaching opportunities include undergraduate and graduate management courses aligned with departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. Candidates interested in developing courses related to artificial intelligence, emerging technologies, innovation, and technology management are particularly encouraged to apply. Additional information can be found in the Management course descriptions . The department emphasizes active and experiential learning, connecting management concepts with real organizational and entrepreneurial challenges through case studies, projects, simulations, competitions, and business and community partnerships. We especially value faculty who enjoy mentoring students, encouraging entrepreneurial thinking, and connecting classroom learning with professional practice. An interest in incorporating data, analytics, and emerging technologies into management education is a plus. Scholarship: The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an active scholarly agenda and contribute to the intellectual life of the department and College. We value meaningful scholarship that informs management practice, advances academic research, and connects with teaching and student learning. We particularly welcome research interests in entrepreneurship, strategy, innovation, technology management, artificial intelligence, and the organizational implications of emerging technologies. Collaborative and interdisciplinary research across business and technology disciplines is encouraged. Responsibilities: Advise and mentor undergraduate and/or graduate students; Contribute to curriculum development, course revision, assessment, and continuous program improvement; Participate actively in departmental, college, and university service; Support experiential learning; Contribute to the intellectual and collegial life of the department; and Support the continued development and visibility of the department’s programs. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Management, with a specialization in Entrepreneurship, Strategic Management, Innovation, or a closely related management discipline, from an AACSB-accredited institution, completed by the start of the appointment. Evidence of, or strong potential for, excellence in university-level teaching aligned with the candidate's expertise. Demonstrated commitment to student engagement, mentoring, and experiential learning. Evidence of, or potential for, maintaining an active program of scholarly research. Candidates who are ABD will be considered, provided there is strong evidence that all doctoral requirements will be completed before the start of the appointment. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Evidence of teaching effectiveness, if available. Contact information for three professional references. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, followed by on-campus interviews for selected candidates. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Michael Zhang, at ZhangM@sacredheart.edu . Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $96,324-$135,986. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 96,324 USD Hiring Max Rate 135,986 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8364": {
      "title": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant Professor Req #943 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 12, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences in the College of Health Professions invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor. We seek an educator-scholar committed to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, scholarly research, and service who will contribute to student success, the advancement of the discipline, and the continued development of our academic programs. This 10-month faculty appointment offers the opportunity to engage with undergraduate and graduate students, contribute to curriculum development and program assessment, and pursue scholarly interests within a collaborative academic environment. The successful candidate will support student learning and professional development while contributing to the College’s mission and the broader University community. Responsibilities: Teach assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses using effective, evidence-based, and inclusive teaching approaches appropriate to the discipline and course format. Contribute to course and curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement. Advise and mentor students in academic planning, professional development, and career preparation, including supervision of scholarly, capstone, practicum, internship, or other experiential learning activities, as appropriate. Establish and maintain an active program of scholarship and/or creative activity, including dissemination of scholarly work and pursuit of internal or external funding, as appropriate. Participate in departmental, College, University, and professional service, including faculty governance, committees, accreditation activities, and related initiatives. Support student recruitment, retention, engagement, and academic success. Maintain current disciplinary and pedagogical expertise through ongoing professional development. Foster an inclusive, collaborative, and collegial academic environment that supports student learning and upholds professional and academic standards. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. or imminent ABD with expected completion by August 2027 in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences or related field. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $95,659-$135,048. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 95,659 USD Hiring Max Rate 135,048 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
