    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8356": {
      "title": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant or Associate Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences - Assistant or Associate Professor Req #944 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 12, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Speech, Language & Hearing Sciences in the College of Health Professions invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor. We seek an educator-scholar committed to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, scholarly research, and service who will contribute to the continued development of our academic programs and the advancement of speech-language pathology and hearing sciences. This 10-month faculty appointment offers the opportunity to engage with undergraduate and graduate students, contribute to curriculum development and program assessment, and pursue scholarly interests within a collaborative academic environment. The successful candidate will support student learning and professional development while contributing to the College’s mission and the broader University community. This is an open-rank position, with the appointment level determined by the candidate’s qualifications and the applicable criteria outlined in the Faculty Handbook. Responsibilities: Provide high-quality instruction in assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses using effective, evidence-based, and inclusive teaching approaches appropriate to the discipline and course format. Contribute to course and curriculum development, program improvement, and assessment of student learning. Advise and mentor students in their academic progress, professional development, and career preparation, including supervision of scholarly, capstone, practicum, internship, or other experiential learning activities, as appropriate. Maintain an active program of scholarship and/or creative activity, including dissemination of scholarly work and pursuit of internal or external funding, as appropriate. Participate in departmental, College, University, and professional service, including faculty governance, committees, accreditation activities, and related initiatives. Support student recruitment, retention, engagement, and academic success. Maintain and advance disciplinary and pedagogical expertise through ongoing professional development and engagement with the profession. Foster an inclusive, collaborative, and collegial academic environment that supports student learning and upholds professional and academic standards. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences or a related field. College or university level teaching experience, particularly in speech-language pathology. Established or emerging scholarly expertise in an area related to speech-language pathology and/or hearing sciences. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $95,659-$135,048. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 95,659 USD Hiring Max Rate 135,048 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
