    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8346": {
      "title": "Horizons - Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Horizons - Administrative Assistant | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Horizons - Administrative Assistant Req #940 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Monday, October 12, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Administrative Assistant provides daily administrative support for Horizons Sacred Heart University, a year-round program serving Bridgeport students and families across its PreK–12 continuum. The position serves as a primary point of contact for families and campus partners and coordinates family communications, admissions and re-enrollment processes, purchasing, program schedules and records, and meeting and event logistics. The Administrative Assistant maintains accurate information, tracks deadlines, and refers decisions and approvals to the Executive Director or appropriate Program Manager. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Family communications: Monitor shared inboxes, phone calls, and inquiries; answer routine questions using approved information; draft, proofread, and distribute family notices through ParentSquare and other approved channels; maintain contact lists and communication logs; refer sensitive matters and policy exceptions to the appropriate leader. Admissions and re-enrollment: Schedule admissions appointments, family meetings, and orientations; distribute and track applications, consent forms, and enrollment and re-enrollment materials; follow up on missing items; maintain applicant records and waitlists; and prepare enrollment status reports. Program leaders make admissions, placement, and exception decisions. Purchasing and supplies: Collect approved supply requests, obtain quotes when needed, enter orders through SHU systems, track deliveries and inventory, and submit invoices and supporting records for review. Purchasing and vendor commitments remain subject to the Executive Director’s approval and SHU procedures. Program scheduling and records: Maintain student schedules and program rosters; communicate approved assignments to families and staff; prepare program materials and spaces; record attendance; and coordinate assessment schedules and materials. Maintain program calendars, student records, and routine reports. Carry out this work under the direction of the Program Managers, who make decisions about student services and programming. Meetings and events: Schedule meetings and maintain event timelines, invitations, RSVP lists, materials, and follow-up tasks. Coordinate logistics for the annual benefit, family activities, Board meetings, and outreach in partnership with University Advancement and SHU Events. The Executive Director retains responsibility for messaging, fundraising, sponsor commitments, and event budgets. Campus and office coordination: Reserve rooms and submit facilities, IT, catering, and other campus service requests; coordinate with SHU departments and vendors on approved logistics; maintain organized shared files; and track administrative forms and renewal deadlines. Other duties: Support special projects and perform related administrative tasks as assigned by the Executive Director. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes High school diploma or equivalent required Experience in an educational or nonprofit setting helpful. Strong written and verbal communication, organization, accuracy, follow-through, discretion, and ability to manage multiple deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Outlook; ability to learn ParentSquare, Salesforce, SHU purchasing systems, and student or donor record systems. Ability to work respectfully with families, students, colleagues, and campus partners; occasional evening or weekend support for scheduled program events may be required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $42,770-$52,729 Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Administrative Support Pay Type Salary Education Level High School Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8487": {
      "title": "Healthcare Informatics & Administration (Onground) - Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Healthcare Informatics & Administration (Onground) - Adjunct Instructor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Healthcare Informatics & Administration (Onground) - Adjunct Instructor Req #28 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA This job posting is no longer available Job Description Posted Sunday, October 25, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expired Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Healthcare Informatics & Administration program in the College of Health Professions invites applications for Adjunct Instructors to teach graduate-level courses in healthcare informatics and related disciplines. Through well-designed curriculum, the Program prepares students for leadership roles in the complex and dynamic healthcare informatics field. We are committed to academic excellence and to cultivating leadership, integrity, and developing engaged citizenship in our students, faculty, staff, and alumni. Through this mission, we will advance the quality and safety of healthcare through the effective use of information technology. Courses are taught in person at Sacred Heart University's Center for Healthcare Education in Bridgeport, Connecticut. This dedicated healthcare education setting offers adjunct instructors the opportunity to share their expertise with graduate students preparing to lead in an increasingly technology-driven healthcare landscape. Explore the Healthcare Informatics curriculum to learn more about the courses offered. Responsibilities: Prepare for and teach assigned graduate-level courses using the approved curriculum and established course objectives Support students in achieving course learning outcomes through effective instruction, engagement, and academic guidance Maintain course materials in Blackboard, including syllabi, assignments, grading rubrics, and other required resources Evaluate student work, provide timely feedback, and maintain accurate grades and attendance records in accordance with University policies Respond to student inquiries within 48 hours and remain reasonably available to meet with students as needed Encourage active student participation and foster an inclusive, respectful, and supportive learning environment Communicate with the Program Chair regarding course delivery, student progress, and academic concerns Fulfill other responsibilities associated with assigned courses Qualifications: An earned master's degree in Informatics, Healthcare Informatics, or a closely related field aligned with the assigned course content Demonstrated practical knowledge, subject-matter expertise, and hands-on experience in the field Strong interpersonal, customer service, presentation, and communication skills Creative thinking, innovation, and effective problem-solving skills Strong organizational skills and the ability to complete assignments accurately and on time with minimal supervision Prior college-level teaching experience is preferred The successful candidate will contribute to a collegial environment and demonstrate a commitment to the University's mission and values, fostering a learning community in which all students can thrive and succeed. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, and relevant examples from courses taught (if applicable). Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide one formal letter of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree. Review of applications will be ongoing based on the needs of the department. All application materials must be submitted through Sacred Heart University’s online application portal. Questions regarding this opportunity may be directed to Dr. Stephen Burrows, Department Chair, burrowss@sacredheart.edu . Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $4,300–$5,400 per 3-credit course. Adjunct Instructors are not eligible to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, they are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Master’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8482": {
      "title": "Information Technology - Senior Billing Specialist, Facilities & Campus Operations",
      "description": "Information Technology - Senior Billing Specialist, Facilities & Campus Operations | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Information Technology - Senior Billing Specialist, Facilities & Campus Operations Req #946 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Thursday, October 22, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Friday, October 30, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Senior Billing Specialist is responsible for managing and coordinating the billing, invoicing, and financial tracking activities for Facilities and Campus Operations. This position ensures accurate processing, coding, approval, and payment of a high volume of invoices related to campus buildings, maintenance projects, utilities, and operational services. The role serves as a key liaison between Facilities departments, Finance, Procurement, and external vendors to ensure financial compliance, budget accuracy, and timely resolution of outstanding invoices and purchase order issues. Primary Duties & Responsibilities Invoice Management & Processing Manage and organize large volumes of invoices across multiple campus buildings and units. Review invoices for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with university policies and contractual agreements. Ensure proper general ledger account coding and departmental charge allocations. Route invoices to appropriate department managers and budget owners for approval and follow-up to ensure timely processing. Maintain accurate records and supporting documentation. Purchase Order Management Monitor and track open purchase orders (POs) for Facilities and Campus Operations departments. Reconcile invoices against purchase orders and contracts to ensure proper authorization and funding availability. Budget Monitoring & Financial Analysis Manage building-level operating budgets to ensure adequate funding is available for planned and ongoing expenditures. Review budget balances and spending trends and proactively notify managers of potential funding concerns. Assist department leaders in forecasting expenditures and tracking financial performance. Generate and maintain budget reports, commitment summaries, and expenditure analyses for Facilities leadership. Research & Resolution of Outstanding Invoices Investigate and resolve outstanding, disputed, or unpaid invoices with vendors, department managers, Procurement, and Accounts Payable. Maintain tracking systems to ensure timely resolution of pending financial transactions. Financial Controls & Compliance Ensure compliance with university financial policies, accounting standards, and procurement procedures. Recommend process improvements to enhance billing accuracy, efficiency, and financial accountability. Assist in developing and maintaining departmental financial procedures and best practices. Other Duties Support other departmental initiatives as assigned by the IT Procurement Manager or Executive Director. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field is preferred. Minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible experience in billing, accounts payable, financial operations, or facilities administration. Experience managing high-volume invoices and purchase orders in a complex organizational environment. Strong understanding of accounting principles, budgeting, and financial reconciliation. Proficiency with ERP, financial management, and procurement systems. Advanced skills in Microsoft Excel and financial reporting tools. Exceptional organizational skills with strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet strict deadlines. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to independently investigate and resolve complex billing and payment issues. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to collaborate effectively with vendors, department leaders, procurement professionals, and accounting personnel. Demonstrated ability to manage confidential financial information with discretion. Strong customer service orientation and commitment to operational excellence. Unusual Working Conditions Must be available to work certain weekends/evenings at various times throughout the year. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $52,000-$65,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Information Technology Pay Type Salary Scan this QR code and apply! Download 3135 Easton Turnpike, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8463": {
      "title": "Graduate Nursing FNP - Visiting Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor",
      "description": "Graduate Nursing FNP - Visiting Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor  | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Graduate Nursing FNP - Visiting Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor Req #949 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Davis & Henley College of Nursing (DHCON) invites applications for a 12-month visiting faculty appointment at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, with primary teaching responsibilities in the online Family Nurse Practitioner (MSN-FNP) program and post-master’s certificate programs, including the Post-MSN Family Nurse Practitioner Certificate . This appointment offers the opportunity to bring your current FNP clinical experience into graduate nursing education through teaching and semester-based student advising. The position is remote, with required travel to campus at least twice annually and as requested by the department chair. The successful candidate will contribute to a college environment grounded in mutual respect and collegiality, value the University’s Catholic identity, tradition, and spirit, and support its commitments to community service, strategic planning, and the intellectual and ethical development of all students. Responsibilities: Teach in the online Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) program and associated post-master’s certificate programs. Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of courses, curricula, and academic programs, including assessment of student learning. Provide student advising each semester. Maintain current FNP clinical practice. Contribute to an inclusive, collaborative, and collegial academic and clinical environment that supports student learning, respects diverse perspectives, and upholds professional and academic standards. Travel to campus at least twice per year and as requested by the department chair. Qualifications: Earned doctorate in nursing. Current RN and APRN licensure. National board certification as a Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP); Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) certification preferred. At least two years of FNP experience and current FNP clinical practice. Previous online graduate teaching experience. Evidence of scholarship. Experience leading an academic team and meeting accreditation and academic nurse practitioner standards. Leadership experience in curriculum development and program administration preferred. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through Sacred Heart University's online application portal: A letter of application outlining relevant qualifications, experience, and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests. Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree will be required upon offer of employment. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $106,179-$149,899. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Travel Required Yes Travel Percentage 5 Telecommute Percentage 95 Hiring Min Rate 106,179 USD Hiring Max Rate 149,899 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8452": {
      "title": "Integrative Biology - Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Integrative Biology - Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Integrative Biology - Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Req #948 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s Department of Biology invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Integrative Biology. This opportunity brings together research across multiple levels of biological organization, undergraduate teaching, and student mentorship within a collegial and collaborative department. We welcome candidates whose research explores integrative biological questions in areas including, but not limited to, physiology, development, genetics, ecology, and evolution. Interdisciplinary research spanning multiple levels of biological organization is strongly preferred. In this role, you will connect your research with undergraduate learning, engaging students majoring in Biology , Coastal & Marine Science , Molecular & Cellular Biology , Neuroscience , or Biomedical Science in your area of expertise. You will join colleagues dedicated to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and experiential learning. Responsibilities: Conduct research addressing integrative biological questions across multiple levels of biological organization that is suitable for undergraduate student involvement. Teach one or more courses in the Biology core curriculum, potentially including Concepts in Biology, Ecology & Evolution, and Genetics & Evolution. Develop upper-level courses in your area of expertise. Contribute positively to the department’s instructional mission and foster an inclusive and supportive learning environment in which all students can thrive. Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biology or a related field in the biological sciences; candidates who are ABD will be considered. Significant teaching and postdoctoral experience preferred. Commitment to supporting the intellectual and ethical development of all students and valuing the University’s Catholic identity, tradition, and spirit. Valid driver’s license. Applications must include: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide: Three formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead Official transcript reflecting the highest conferred degree All application materials must be submitted through the Sacred Heart University Online Application Portal. Review of applications will begin December 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $75,342-$106,366. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Doctorate Hiring Min Rate 75,342 USD Hiring Max Rate 106,366 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8446": {
      "title": "Clinical Coordinator, Diagnostic Medical Sonography",
      "description": "Clinical Coordinator, Diagnostic Medical Sonography - Assistant Clinical Professor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Clinical Coordinator, Diagnostic Medical Sonography - Assistant Clinical Professor Req #947 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre. www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here Sacred Heart University’s College of Health Professions (CHP) invites applications for an Assistant Clinical Professor to serve as a founding faculty member and Clinical Coordinator of the new Diagnostic Medical Sonography program. CHP prepares students for meaningful careers in today’s dynamic healthcare environment through inclusive, collaborative, and experiential learning. Its undergraduate and graduate programs combine state-of-the-art facilities, interprofessional education, and hands-on experiences through advanced simulation, clinical placements, and global service-learning. Guided by the University’s mission, the College fosters excellence, compassion, and a commitment to social justice, community, and the common good. The successful candidate will bring clinical expertise and a commitment to student learning and professional preparation. Responsibilities include teaching, scholarship, advising and mentorship, and service in support of the academic program and the College’s mission. The position contributes to student learning and success, the advancement of the discipline, and the ongoing development of the academic program and University community. As a founding faculty member, you will help build and shape the program through curriculum development and implementation, clinical partnership development, accreditation activities, student recruitment, and program growth. The faculty member will also serve as a Specialty Concentration Coordinator, providing leadership for curriculum and student learning experiences within their area of professional expertise, in accordance with program and accreditation requirements. These responsibilities may vary based on professional credentials, expertise, and program needs. As Clinical Coordinator, the faculty member will oversee clinical education and student clinical experiences, develop and maintain partnerships with affiliated clinical sites, and serve as a key liaison between the academic program and clinical partners. About the Diagnostic Medical Sonography Program: The new Diagnostic Medical Sonography (DMS) program at Sacred Heart University will welcome its first cohort in Fall 2027. The undergraduate program will prepare students for professional practice through classroom instruction, hands-on laboratory education, and clinical experiences. The curriculum will focus on developing the knowledge and clinical skills needed for successful, patient-centered professional practice in diagnostic medical sonography. Responsibilities: Provide high-quality instruction in assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses, including Diagnostic Medical Sonography courses, using effective, evidence-based, and inclusive pedagogical approaches appropriate to the discipline and course modality. Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of courses, curricula, and academic programs, including assessment of student learning. Advise and mentor students in support of academic progress, professional development, career preparation, and preparation for professional practice. Supervise students in appropriate scholarly, capstone, practicum, internship, or other experiential learning activities. Maintain and advance disciplinary and pedagogical expertise through ongoing professional development, engagement with the profession, and current clinical practice, as appropriate to the faculty member’s role. Engage in active and meaningful service to the department/program, College, University, and profession, including faculty governance, committee work, accreditation activities, and other initiatives aligned with the faculty member’s expertise and role. Contribute to the implementation, development, and continuous improvement of the Diagnostic Medical Sonography program, including curriculum refinement, student recruitment, accreditation preparation, assessment activities, and program growth initiatives. Participate in recruitment and outreach activities that support program and College enrollment goals, student retention, engagement, and success. Contribute to an inclusive, collaborative, and collegial academic and clinical environment that supports student learning, respects diverse perspectives, and upholds professional and academic standards. Serve as the Specialty Concentration Coordinator, providing concentration-specific leadership and oversight in accordance with program and accreditation requirements. Responsibilities may vary based on the faculty member’s professional credentials, area of expertise, and program needs. Clinical Education Responsibilities: Coordinate and oversee the clinical education component of the Diagnostic Medical Sonography program in collaboration with the Program Director and program faculty, ensuring alignment with program goals, student learning outcomes, and applicable Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs (CAAHEP) and Joint Review Committee on Education in Diagnostic Medical Sonography (JRC-DMS) requirements. Ensure appropriate integration among didactic, laboratory, and clinical education and support students’ progression toward required competencies. Establish, maintain, and evaluate clinical education partnerships, including identifying and assessing clinical sites. Ensure affiliated sites provide appropriate supervision, resources, patient populations, procedures, and learning opportunities for students to achieve required competencies. Monitor the quality and effectiveness of clinical education experiences and address site needs or concerns in collaboration with clinical partners and program faculty. Coordinate student clinical placements and serve as a primary liaison between the academic program and clinical sites, considering student readiness, site capacity, program requirements, and opportunities for progressive clinical learning. Maintain effective communication with students, clinical instructors, program faculty, and relevant University offices regarding clinical requirements, schedules, expectations, student performance, progression, and affiliation needs. Coordinate clinical instructor orientation and support by providing guidance and resources related to student supervision, instruction, assessment, feedback, and documentation, and by facilitating communication between clinical instructors and the academic program. Monitor and support student clinical progression, including participation, competency attainment, performance, and readiness for progression. Identify students requiring additional support and coordinate appropriate remediation or improvement plans in collaboration with the Program Director, faculty, clinical instructors, and appropriate University personnel. Evaluate and continuously improve the clinical education program using student outcomes, student and clinical instructor feedback, site evaluations, and other relevant information to inform clinical education policies, procedures, assessment tools, learning experiences, and accreditation activities. Maintain clinical education records and contribute to program assessment, reporting, accreditation, and continuous improvement activities in accordance with institutional, CAAHEP, and JRC-DMS requirements. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in Diagnostic Medical Sonography, health sciences, education, or a related field. Completion of an accredited Diagnostic Medical Sonography program or equivalent educational preparation. Current and active ARDMS Registered Diagnostic Medical Sonographer (RDMS) credential. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Minimum of two years of full-time clinical experience as a registered sonographer. Experience working with students in a clinical setting, including providing instruction, supervision, feedback, and evaluation of clinical performance. Strong organizational, interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with students, faculty, clinical partners, and healthcare professionals. Ability to establish and sustain clinical education partnerships with healthcare organizations. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in a relevant field or current enrollment in a master’s degree program. Three or more years of clinical experience as a registered diagnostic medical sonographer. Professional expertise or ARDMS credentials in areas such as Musculoskeletal Sonography (RMSKS), Obstetrics and Gynecology (OB/GYN), and/or Vascular Technology (RVT). Experience teaching diagnostic medical sonography in a college or university setting. Experience coordinating clinical education, student clinical rotations, or clinical affiliates within a sonography or allied health program. Familiarity with CAAHEP/JRC-DMS accreditation standards, program assessment, or clinical competency documentation. Experience developing or evaluating curriculum, clinical education, or student learning experiences, particularly in diagnostic medical sonography education. Work Environment and Physical Requirements: This position requires regular on-campus presence, with periodic travel to affiliated clinical education sites and occasional evening or weekend responsibilities. The work may involve sitting and standing for extended periods; positioning and assisting students and/or patients during laboratory and clinical instruction; and operating, positioning, and moving diagnostic medical sonography equipment and other discipline-specific laboratory and clinical technologies. The position also requires the ability to demonstrate sonographic scanning techniques and participate in hands-on laboratory and clinical instruction. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants are invited to submit the following materials through the University’s online application portal: A cover letter addressing their interest in and qualifications for the position, including teaching experience and approach to supporting student learning. A current curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references, including each reference’s name, title, email address, and professional relationship to the applicant. References will be contacted only if the applicant advances to the final round of consideration. Upon offer of employment, the selected candidate will be required to provide formal letters of recommendation on professional letterhead and an official transcript reflecting their highest earned degree in accordance with University policy. All applications must be submitted through the University’s online application portal . Materials submitted via email or other means will not be accepted or reviewed. Only completed applications will be considered. Application review will begin on November 9 . Applications will continue to be accepted and reviewed until the position is filled. Questions regarding this position may be addressed to Stephanie Clines, PhD, LAT, ATC, Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs, at cliness@sacredheart.edu . Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this position is $105,225-$148,553. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Faculty Job Function Faculty Pay Type Salary Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Hiring Min Rate 105,225 USD Hiring Max Rate 148,553 USD Scan this QR code and apply! Download 4000 Park Ave, Bridgeport, CT 06604, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8556": {
      "title": "Jandrisevits Learning Ctr.",
      "description": "Jandrisevits Learning Ctr. - Test Proctor | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Jandrisevits Learning Ctr. - Test Proctor Req #953 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Test Proctor plays a critical role in maintaining the integrity and smooth administration of exams in the Testing Center. This position is responsible for ensuring that all testing procedures are followed, providing support to students with accommodations, and fostering a professional, secure, and inclusive testing environment. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Examinee Readiness Ensure all required check-in and security screening procedures are completed before students enter the testing room. Greet students and verify their identity. Provide exam details, including duration, assigned seating and permitted materials. Conduct security checks to ensure students do not possess unauthorized items. Proctoring & Exam Administration Maintain exam integrity by ensuring all procedures are followed and students are supported throughout testing. Verify student identities, confirm seating arrangements, and monitor students throughout the exam. Communicate time limits and provide periodic time updates. Maintain a quiet and controlled testing environment. Collaborate with the Testing Center Coordinators to address student questions and resolve issues. Keep records of test administration. Assist students with assistive technologies and testing platforms used in the testing center. Remain vigilant in monitoring multiple students for potential academic integrity violations, and document and report any suspected incidents to Testing Center coordinators in accordance with Testing Center policies. Materials Management & Testing Environment Ensure all materials and testing spaces are properly maintained. Maintain confidentiality of student information, including disabilities and accommodations. Safeguard testing materials, logs, and related documents. Distribute and replenish supplies such as pencils, pens, and scratch paper. Keep desks and testing areas clean, organized, and sanitized. Collect completed exams and verify all materials are accounted for through accurate counts. Return completed exams to instructors. All other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes An Associate degree is required; Bachelor's degree is preferred. Strong attention to detail and ability to remain alert for extended periods. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Familiarity with basic computer systems and testing software preferred. Ability to read college-level exam questions verbally. Ability to follow detailed procedures and enforce policies consistently. Unusual Working Conditions Requires prolonged periods of sitting or standing while monitoring exams. Must maintain focus in a quiet, controlled testing environment. May involve interaction with students experiencing test-related stress. May require working during (7:45 AM-12 or 12-4 PM) or/and evening (4-7:30 PM) hours Will work 10-12 hours per week during the regular semester; Up to 20 hours are available during the regular semester for interested candidates, subject to change based on the needs of the University Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits: The hourly compensation for this position ranges from $16.99 - $25.49. Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Hourly Employment Indicator Seasonal <120 Days Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8542": {
      "title": "Notre Dame Prep - Assistant Coach Girl's Basketball",
      "description": "Notre Dame Prep - Assistant Coach Girl's Basketball | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Notre Dame Prep - Assistant Coach Girl's Basketball Req #958 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 9:00 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a cover letter, resume, or curriculum vitae, along with the contact information for three letters of reference, who will be contacted only if you are selected for an interview. Only applications submitted via our Career portal will be considered. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Assistant Coach will work alongside the Head Coach to support the development and coaching of student-athletes at Notre Dame Prep. This position is focused on fostering a positive and competitive environment while promoting academic excellence, physical fitness, and sportsmanship. The Assistant Coach will contribute to the team’s training, development, and performance, helping to ensure that the athletic program aligns with the school’s mission and values. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Assist the Head Coach in planning, organizing, and conducting practices, training sessions, and team events. Provide instruction, feedback, and motivation to student-athletes during practices and competitions. Help develop and implement team strategies, drills, and plays to improve performance. Monitor and ensure that student-athletes follow all school and athletic policies, including academic eligibility and conduct standards. Assist with the evaluation of new student-athletes. Assist with team communications, including emails, announcements, and social media, to keep players and families informed. Help organize and supervise team events, including team-building activities, fundraisers, and special occasions. Support the Head Coach in managing the team’s equipment, uniforms, and other logistical needs. Foster a positive, respectful, and inclusive environment that promotes good sportsmanship, discipline, and teamwork. Attend coaching staff meetings and contribute to the planning and review of the team’s progress throughout the season. Assist with monitoring the health and wellness of student-athletes, ensuring they receive proper care and attention during and after practices or competitions. Provide feedback and recommendations to the Head Coach regarding team performance, individual player progress, and areas for improvement. Represent the school positively and professionally at all times, both on and off the field. Other duties as assigned by the Head Coach or Athletic Director. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Requirements High school diploma or equivalent required; high school athletic experience or coaching certification preferred. At least 1-2 years of coaching or playing experience in the sport, ideally at the high school or collegiate level. Ability to complete and maintain First Aid certification Strong knowledge of the sport, including techniques, rules, and strategies. Ability to communicate effectively with student-athletes, parents, and school staff. Strong leadership skills with the ability to motivate and inspire student-athletes. Ability to work as part of a team and collaborate effectively with the Head Coach and other coaching staff. Organizational skills to manage practice schedules, equipment, and other team logistics. Ability to foster a positive, respectful, and inclusive team environment. Strong commitment to the academic and personal development of student-athletes. Ability to maintain professional conduct at all times, representing Notre Dame Prep both on and off the field. Unusual Working Conditions Evening and weekend hours are often required for practices, games, and team events. Travel to away games, tournaments, or competitions may be required. The position involves physical activity, including standing for extended periods, participating in drills, and demonstrating techniques. Flexibility to assist in multiple roles (e.g., recruiting, event planning) depending on the needs of the team and school. Pre-Employment Requirement All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a fingerprint-supported background check and a DCF/CPS background check. Compensation & Benefits: The salary range for this seasonal position is $2,500 - $3,000. Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Athletics Pay Type Salary Employment Indicator Seasonal <120 Days Travel Required Yes Scan this QR code and apply! Download 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8532": {
      "title": "Immigration Support Services - Director of International & Immigration Services",
      "description": "Immigration Support Services - Director of International & Immigration Services | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Immigration Support Services - Director of International & Immigration Services Req #950 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Saturday, November 28, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary The Director of International and Immigration Services will serve as the PDSO (Principal Designated School Official) for the F1 Program and the RO (Responsible Officer) for the J1 Program in SEVIS for Sacred Heart’s programs and the PDSO for Notre Dame Prep High School, part of Sacred Heart University. Must be a U.S. citizen or permanent resident. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Under the direction of the Executive Director of Graduate & International Student Life, t he Director of International & Immigration Services (PDSO/RO) performs the following duties: Institutional Compliance (30%) Serves as a “Principal Designated School Official” (PDSO) and a “Responsible Officer” (RO) in the Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS) and maintains expertise in F-1 & J-1 visa regulations. Ensures institutional compliance with SEVP regulations by maintaining the I-17 and DS-3036 form accurately and timely updated, by filing recertifications and program changes and updates. Monitors immigration regulations, policy changes, and federal guidance and translates requirements into institutional procedures and communications. Leads all communications with SEVP support and the designated SEVP representative on behalf of the institution. Organizes SEVIS data processing under the guidelines provided by the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and maintains data and quality control management. Provides institutional guidance on F-1 and J-1 regulations, including admissions, enrollment, employment, program changes, transfers, and student status of enrolled, OPT & STEM OPT populations. Student & Community Support on Immigration Compliance (50%) Leads comprehensive immigration advising throughout their academic journey and on post-completion employment. Provides timely guidance on visas, status maintenance, employment authorization, travel, program changes, transfers, and other immigration matters. Develops programs, communication, and resources that promote international student transition, belonging, engagement, and success. Provides accurate immigration information to international students, monitors and tracks student immigration status, and maintains appropriate records. Establishes, updates, and tracks SEVIS records on a semester/trimester/module basis. Prepares and/or coordinates preparation of F-1 documents for undergraduate and graduate programs and ensures compliance with all federal policies and regulations. Serves as liaison to deans, department heads, faculty, and administrators within the University and provides advanced immigration-related advice and assistance to faculty and administrators regarding international student regulations. Develops and maintains an in-depth knowledge of the academic programs, as well as relevant policies and procedures within each academic department to apply immigration regulations accordingly. Advises students with immigration petitions and applications to include processing for new F-1 visas, employment authorizations, reinstatement, and reduced course load authorizations, change of status, and medical leave. Ensures that students maintain OPT and STEM OPT employment authorizations and are informed of all necessary reporting requirements. Coordinates with outside organizations to provide external services for international students, i.e., tax filing, banking services, mobile services, and others. Guides students to help them access appropriate community services and local resources. Assists the Executive Director with the delivery of quality experience and programming to enrolled international students. Staff Supervision & Support (20%) Supervises and supports staff responsible for international student services, immigration advising, and related programs. Provides training and professional development to staff on immigration regulations, SEVIS requirements, advising practices, and emerging issues. Establishes clear procedures, service standards, and workflows to ensure consistent and effective student support. Supervises and trains all DSO’s and ARO’s (Designated School Officials and Assistant Responsible Offices). Supports staff with professional development planning and maintains a relationship with professional organizations to keep abreast of changes in federal rules and regulations. Attends regional or national workshops and conferences to stay current on immigration policies. Other Duties as Assigned Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Master’s degree preferred or commensurate experience. Requires knowledge of SEVIS and F1 and J1 visa regulations with a minimum of 5-7 years of working experience as a PDSO or DSO and RO/ARO. Requires superior communication skills to educate students, university faculty, and administrators on matters related to non-immigrant regulations and institutional policies, as well as the ability to understand and explain complex government regulations and institutional policies to non-native speakers of the English language. Requires the ability to maintain detailed immigration records, perform intricate immigration processing, and ensure institutional compliance with student immigration regulations. Requires patience, professionalism, and a high level of sensitivity when advising students. Unusual Working Conditions In-person position; some weekend and night hours might be required, especially during semester orientation weeks and the start of the academic year. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $80,000-$95,000. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Salary Education Level Master’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8515": {
      "title": "Public Safety",
      "description": "Public Safety - Officer | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Public Safety - Officer Req #952 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Wednesday, November 4, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary To provide for the safety and security of all University community members, to provide for the physical security of University property, and to enforce University rules and regulations. To provide a variety of Public Safety services in a professional and timely manner by proactively patrolling University properties and responding to calls for service as assigned. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Patrols University properties via foot, bicycle, or vehicle, as assigned. Provides a dedicated security presence at an assigned post/location. Performs Dispatcher duties as required. Provides proactive services as necessary Enforces University policies and procedures within the University community with regard to security and public safety Adheres to the Department of Public Safety rules, regulations, responsibilities, and procedures Complies with and is respectful of Supervisors and their instructions, directives, and assignments Submits Incident Reports documenting any unusual occurrence, complaint, and/or crime/incident in a timely manner; investigates as appropriate Maintains a professional, formal, and approachable demeanor while on duty and engages in effective public relations when interacting with the University community. Interacts professionally with all internal University Departments and external municipal partners (police, fire, ambulance, etc.) Respond to and investigate incidents or emergencies as assigned, including, but not limited to, fire alarms/fires, medical incidents, weather emergencies, motor vehicle accidents, disturbances, etc. Provide Public Safety services to the University community, including personal safety escorts, motor vehicle assistance, room/bldg. unlocks, bank runs, etc. Enforces parking rules and regulations on all campus properties Takes timely and appropriate actions, including requesting other assistance as may needed Will not act, either on duty or off duty, in any manner that is detrimental, in the view of SHU, to the Mission or reputation of SHU Essential physical job tasks: Sitting, standing, or walking for sustained periods of time, Climbing up/down stairs, Bending, turning, reaching, and grasping, Visual acuity sufficient for reading ID cards/written materials and making general observations Hearing sufficient for perceiving sounds at normal speaking levels Works special assignments and shifts as directed Perform other duties as directed Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent CT State Security Guard Card (or eligible to obtain card) Be in good physical condition with height and weight in proportion Possess a valid driver’s license Possess and maintain a clean criminal history and driving record No felony convictions Must not have been dismissed from any law enforcement unit for malfeasance or other serious misconduct. Must not have resigned or retired from any law enforcement position while under investigation for any malfeasance or misconduct. Preferred Qualifications Prior Law Enforcement experience strongly encouraged Associate's degree or Bachelor’s Degree preferred Experience with Microsoft Office products; ability to type 40-60 words per minute EMR or EMT license, CPR & First Aid certifications Knowledge & experience using CAD software or public safety dispatching certifications Unusual Working Conditions Public Safety Officers are assigned to shift work and may be required to work all shifts (nights, weekends, and holidays) as needed. They may also be required to work overtime based on operational needs. They must be capable of performing professionally under stressful situations and may be required to work in adverse weather conditions. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes § 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $20.25-$20.96. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Hourly Education Level High School Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8507": {
      "title": "Great River Golf Club - Assistant Superintendent in Training",
      "description": "Great River Golf Club - Assistant Superintendent in Training | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Great River Golf Club - Assistant Superintendent in Training Req #932 130 Coram Ln, Milford, CT 06461, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Saturday, November 28, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position Position Summary Assist the Superintendent and Assistant Superintendent daily and be responsible for maintaining the facilities and grounds at Great River Golf Course. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Assistant the Assistant Superintendent and Superintendent with daily scheduling and planning Lead and manage small teams in the completion of projects. Daily course setup: creating pin location sheets, moving pins, and moving tee locations. Perform preventative maintenance of facilities and buildings. Perform routine maintenance tasks such as mowing, trimming, and edging to keep the golf course and surrounding areas neat and well-groomed. Maintain golf course features, including tees, greens, fairways, roughs, bunkers, cart paths, and parking lot areas to ensure they meet established standards. Perform duties utilizing rakes, shovels, brooms, and various hand tools. Irrigation and water management, including understanding watering principles and techniques, repairing and adjusting sprinkler systems as needed. Perform special tasks related to drainage, tree maintenance, and course construction and shaping. Engage in landscaping tasks such as planting, pruning, weeding, mulching, and filling divots to enhance the course's natural beauty. Assist with golf course renovation projects, including aerating, seeding, and sodding. Monitor the course for any signs of damage or wear and promptly report issues to the supervisor. Operate and maintain various groundskeeping equipment, such as walk-behind mowers, blowers, backpack blowers, and string trimmers, ensuring tools are clean, safe, and in good working order. Operate and maintain heavy equipment, such as backhoes, skid steers, Ventrac tractors, and tractors, as directed. Operate a golf cart. Provide exceptional customer service by interacting professionally with members and guests and addressing any concerns or questions related to the course conditions. Perform other duties as assigned by the Golf Course Superintendent or management. Assists the snow removal team during the winter months with shoveling sidewalks, decks, & patios. Operates snow removal equipment, including trucks, skid steers, tractors, & loaders. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, & Other Attributes There are no formal education requirements; a high school diploma or equivalent is preferred. A valid driver’s license with no current violations is required. Knowledge of golf rules and golf course etiquette is preferred. Previous experience in landscaping, golf course groundskeeping, or related fields is preferred. Demonstrated ability to operate groundskeeping equipment safely, including lawnmowers, trimmers, and blowers. Demonstrated ability to operate heavy equipment safely, including backhoes, skid steers, Ventrac tractors, and tractors. Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining high course appearance and functionality standards. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Must be able to perform manual labor tasks, including lifting up to 50 pounds, carrying, pushing, pulling, bending, stooping, stretching, twisting, reaching with arms and/or legs, and walking extensively throughout the day. Willingness and ability to work in various outdoor environmental and weather conditions, including exposure to insects, pests, and varying temperatures. Ability to understand and communicate written and verbal instructions accurately. Must be dependable and punctual; arrive on time and prepared to start working. Willing to stay late and arrive early as needed. Be forward-thinking and bring new ideas to elevate our current product. Strong work ethic and attention to detail. Unusual Working Conditions Availability to work early mornings, weekends, and holidays as required by the golf course schedule. Duties require physical strength, standing, and endurance in various weather conditions for extended periods outdoors and lifting 50+ pounds at times. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. In accordance with Connecticut General Statutes § 31-51v, applicants selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment drug test as a condition of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory results of both the background check and drug test. Compensation & Benefits : The annual salary range for this position is $22.00-$30.00. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Pay Type Hourly Scan this QR code and apply! Download 130 Coram Ln, Milford, CT 06461, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8581": {
      "title": "Notre Dame Prep - Administrative Assistant, Guidance Office",
      "description": "Notre Dame Prep - Administrative Assistant, Guidance Office | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Notre Dame Prep - Administrative Assistant, Guidance Office Req #955 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 9:00 PM T o apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a cover letter, resume, or curriculum vitae, along with the contact information for three letters of reference, who will be contacted only if you are selected for an interview. Only applications submitted via our Career portal will be considered. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary The Administrative Assistant plays a key role in ensuring the smooth and efficient operation of the school’s administrative functions. This position provides clerical and administrative support to school leadership, counselors, teachers, and staff, assisting with a wide range of tasks including scheduling, communication, record-keeping, and office management. The Administrative Assistant helps maintain a welcoming, organized environment and ensures office operations run effectively and efficiently Principal Duties & Responsibilities Answer and direct phone calls in the Guidance Office, take messages, and assist students, parents, and visitors with general inquiries, ensuring excellent customer service; Assist students, parents, and college representatives in accessing counselors and support services; Prepare and distribute correspondence, reports, and documents for the counselors; perform data entry, filing, and general document management; Provide administrative support for school committees, special projects, and events as directed by the Principal or school leadership; Maintain office supplies and equipment, ensuring inventory is stocked and in working order; Maintain and organize student, staff, attendance, and counseling records in compliance with privacy policies, including daily secure storage; Process transcript requests and send academic records for students withdrawing from Notre Dame Prep; Ensure receipt and proper recording of summer school grades; Using Naviance, support college application processes by ensuring student records are complete and submitted on time; Assist students with college and scholarship applications as needed; Process student requests for Working Papers; Schedule college rep visits; Support the administration of standardized testing on school days as needed; Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes High school diploma required; associate’s degree or equivalent experience preferred. At least 2 years of experience in an administrative or clerical role, preferably within a school or educational environment. The role requires flexibility to adapt to the changing needs of the school and its staff. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to interact professionally with students, staff, and parents. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and other office software. Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously. Ability to handle sensitive information confidentially and professionally. Excellent customer service skills, with the ability to remain calm and professional in a busy office environment. Ability to work independently and take initiative, while also being a supportive team player. A positive and proactive attitude, with a willingness to learn and contribute to the school’s success. Unusual Working Conditions Occasional evenings or weekend work may be required for school events, meetings, or special projects. Dynamic and fast-paced work environment, particularly during peak times (e.g., start of school year, parent-teacher conferences). Pre-Employment Requirement All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a fingerprint-supported background check and a DCF/CPS background check. Compensation & Benefits: The hourly compensation for this position ranges from $20.56 - $27.40. Sacred Heart University offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life insurance, disability, retirement, paid time off, tuition remission, and other employee benefits. Specific benefits and eligibility requirements may vary based on the position and applicable plan provisions. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Administrative Support Pay Type Hourly Travel Required No Scan this QR code and apply! Download 220 Jefferson St, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    },
    "https://jobs.dayforcehcm.com/en-US/shu/CANDIDATEPORTAL/jobs/8571": {
      "title": "Marketing & Communications - Temporary Marketing Manager",
      "description": "Marketing & Communications - Temporary Marketing Manager | Dayforce Jobs Skip to Content Search Jobs Recommended Jobs English (United States) Sign In Marketing & Communications - Temporary Marketing Manager Req #941 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA Apply Share Job Description Posted Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 9:00 PM | Expires Sunday, November 29, 2026 at 8:59 PM About Sacred Heart University As one of the nation’s largest Catholic universities and among the fastest-growing private doctoral institutions in the U.S., Sacred Heart University is a national leader in shaping higher education for the 21st century. SHU offers more than 100 undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs on its Fairfield, Conn., campus. Sacred Heart also has a campus in Dingle, Ireland, and offers online programs. Nearly 10,000 students attend the University’s nine colleges and schools: College of Arts & Sciences; School of Communication, Media & the Arts; School of Social Work; School of Computing & Engineering; School of Performing Arts; College of Health Professions; the Isabelle Farrington College of Education & Human Development; the Jack Welch College of Business & Technology; and the Dr. Susan L. Davis, RN, & Richard J. Henley College of Nursing. Sacred Heart, a Laudato Si’ campus, stands out from other Catholic universities as it was established to be led by the laity. This contemporary Catholic university is rooted in the rich Catholic intellectual tradition and the liberal arts and, at the same time, cultivates students to be forward thinkers who enact change in their own lives, professions, and communities. Sacred Heart University has earned national recognition for academic excellence, student success, career outcomes, and campus experience. The Princeton Review recognized SHU in its Best 392 Colleges: 2027 Edition and Best Business Schools: 2027 Edition, while additional national recognitions highlight the University’s commitment to preparing students for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Sacred Heart is home to the award-winning, NPR-affiliate station, WSHU Public Radio; Division I athletics; and an impressive performing arts program that includes choir, band, dance, and theatre . www.sacredheart.edu View SHU’s Faculty Experts Here To apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a completed application and résumé through the University's online application system. Applications submitted outside of the official Careers at SHU website will not be considered. Applicants should not apply through third-party or external job sites, as such postings may be fraudulent or may misrepresent opportunities that are no longer available at the University. A cover letter or statement of interest is preferred for all staff positions. Sacred Heart University complies with all federal and state employment laws and regulations. Applicants must be lawfully authorized to work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa for this position. Position Summary Provide overall support to the Marketing and Communications department, managing efforts to support graduate enrollment goals. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Support the Executive Director of Marketing in the execution of marketing strategies and initiatives designed to advance graduate enrollment goals across Sacred Heart University’s colleges and graduate programs. Partner with Strategic Enrollment Management (SEM), Graduate Admissions, and faculty to understand graduate program priorities, target audiences, differentiators, enrollment goals, and recruitment needs and translate them into effective marketing content and initiatives. Coordinate content updates for graduate program, department, and other enrollment-focused webpages. Ensure content is accurate, current, compelling, accessible, and optimized for prospective students. Support the marketing and promotion of graduate recruitment events, including open houses, virtual information sessions, webinars and other enrollment initiatives. Provide marketing oversight for graduate print collateral, including program fact sheets, brochures, postcards, event materials and other recruitment pieces. Partner with writers, designers and University stakeholders throughout content development, review and production. Review graduate digital advertising creative and messaging, including Google search and display advertising, and provide recommendations to strengthen message alignment, program positioning and prospective-student relevance. Provide strategic direction for graduate-focused video and photography projects. Coordinate academic photo and video shoots with faculty, students, University partners and creative teams to build compelling visual assets that support graduate recruitment. Identify opportunities to strengthen graduate program storytelling and proof points. Conduct outreach to students, alumni and faculty to gather testimonials and success stories for use across web, digital, print and other marketing channels. Collaborate with Communications and Social Media teams to identify and amplify graduate academic achievements, faculty expertise, student outcomes and other stories that support University awareness, reputation and enrollment goals. Manage assigned graduate marketing projects through Asana, coordinating stakeholders, timelines, approvals and deliverables to ensure projects remain on schedule. Serve as a steward of the Sacred Heart University brand, ensuring graduate marketing materials and communications adhere to University brand, editorial and messaging standards. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned in support of Marketing & Communications and graduate enrollment priorities. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities & Other Attributes Bachelor's Degree in Marketing/Communications or a related field. Ability to own projects, communicate with various University stakeholders, work with creative teams, and deliver projects on budget and on time. Demonstrated success in marketing or enrollment fields. A particular understanding of content development, strategy, and execution through multiple channels, including social media, digital media advertising, and web management. Understanding of how the online world can assist in meeting goals. Utilizing Excel is a must. Ability to use project management software such as Asana is required. Must be willing to work against tight deadlines while balancing multiple projects at once. Sound ethical decision-making skills, enthusiasm, and respect for confidential issues. Highly organized, detail-oriented, resourceful, and accountable to schedules. Excellent communication skills. Must demonstrate strong writing, editorial, and proofreading skills. Collaborator/Liaison. Must be a proactive communicator and a team player, eager and able to anticipate and uncover new opportunities and needs. Should have a personality that facilitates active collaboration with internal departments to support and produce marketing materials. Also acts as steward of the SHU brand identity. Unusual Working Conditions Evening and weekend hours may be required. Pre-Employment Requirements All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check. Compensation & Benefits : The hourly compensation for this position ranges from $28.00-$33.00. Non-benefit eligible employees are unable to participate in the University’s employee health and welfare benefit programs; however, part-time, non-benefit eligible employees are eligible to participate in Sacred Heart University’s 403(b) retirement plan, but they are not eligible to receive the employer matching contributions, subject to the terms and eligibility requirements of the plan. Temporary, per-diem, and seasonal staff are not eligible to participate in the 403(b) retirement plan. This job posting provides an overview of the role's general nature and expected tasks. It is not meant to be a comprehensive list of all duties performed. The university reserves the right to modify or reassign job responsibilities at any time. This posting description does not constitute an employment contract, either explicit or implied. Sacred Heart University is a space that respects and embraces differences, recognizes the unique contributions that individuals can make, and creates a community that maximizes the potential of all faculty and staff. As an equal opportunity employer, we encourage applications from qualified candidates who reflect the wider world in which we live. Job Details Job Family Staff Job Function Marketing & Communications Pay Type Hourly Education Level Bachelor’s Degree Scan this QR code and apply! Download 5151 Park Ave, Fairfield, CT 06825, USA ©2009-2026 Dayforce HCM, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Cookie Preferences Cookie Preferences We use technology, such as cookies, to improve site functionality, personalize content, and analyze web traffic. By clicking \"Accept\" you also allow optional advertising, analytics, and candidate conversion tracking. You can learn more about online tracking in our Cookie Statement Accept Reject Cookie Settings"
    }
